      "html": "<figure class=\"explain-figure early-figure\" id=\"visual-E06\" data-early=\"E06\" lang=\"en\"><header><span>E06</span><h3>Equal values can be measured together</h3></header><p class=\"\">The same value may occur in separated places. Group those places and add value × measure.</p><div class=\"early-flow\"><section><h4>Spatial order</h4><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v1/E06-en-domain-0.svg\" alt=\"Eight equal cells with three values\" data-domain></section><div class=\"flow-arrow\">→</div><section><h4>Group by value</h4><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v1/E06-en-values-0.svg\" alt=\"Equal-value regions have measures 3/8,2/8,3/8\" data-values></section></div><div class=\"e06-mobile\"><h4>Spatial order ↓ group by value</h4><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v1/E06-en-mobile-0.svg\" alt=\"Compact grouped measure diagram\" data-mobile-group></div><div class=\"v5-controls\" role=\"group\"><button type=\"button\" data-value=\"0\" aria-pressed=\"true\">All</button><button type=\"button\" data-value=\"1\" aria-pressed=\"false\">f=1</button><button type=\"button\" data-value=\"3\" aria-pressed=\"false\">f=3</button><button type=\"button\" data-value=\"5\" aria-pressed=\"false\">f=5</button></div><p class=\"early-result\">3/8 + 6/8 + 15/8 = 3</p><output data-reading>Add the three contributions; the original function is unchanged.</output><figcaption id=\"visual-E06-end\">Model: eight equal half-open cells in [0,1], with 1 included in the last cell, have values 1,5,1,3,5,1,3,5. The right panel rearranges the measures of equal-value sets into contiguous bands; it does not assert that the original sets are contiguous. Their measurable preimages have measures 3/8,2/8,3/8; the integral is 3. Clicking highlights a group without changing the function or measure. This explains a simple-function sum, not the full construction of Lebesgue integration. This finite step function is also Riemann integrable; the failure example is the text’s Dirichlet function.</figcaption><nav class=\"ex-downloads\"><a href=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v1/E06.en.svg\">Complete static SVG</a><a href=\"/print/E06.en.html\">Print view</a></nav></figure>",
