      "title": "Choose a family, or choose an individual?",
      "html": "<figure class=\"explain-figure early-figure\" id=\"visual-E20\" data-early=\"E20\" lang=\"en\"><header><span>E20</span><h3>Choose a family, or choose an individual?</h3></header><p class=\"\">Two family types originally have equal probability. Choosing a family first differs from weighting families by their number of children.</p><div class=\"v5-controls\" role=\"group\"><button type=\"button\" data-family-law=\"P\" aria-pressed=\"true\">Equal family weights</button><button type=\"button\" data-family-law=\"Q\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Population-weighted families</button></div><div class=\"early-single wide\"><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v1/E20-en-P-1.svg\" alt=\"Fixed trees with probability areas and one marked ancestor line\" data-family-scene></div><div class=\"v5-controls\" role=\"group\"><button type=\"button\" data-child=\"0\" aria-pressed=\"false\">A₁</button><button type=\"button\" data-child=\"1\" aria-pressed=\"true\">B₁</button><button type=\"button\" data-child=\"2\" aria-pressed=\"false\">B₂</button><button type=\"button\" data-child=\"3\" aria-pressed=\"false\">B₃</button></div><output data-reading>Original family weights 1/2: joint child weights 1/2,1/6,1/6,1/6.</output><figcaption id=\"visual-E20-end\">Exact first-generation example: P(L=1)=P(L=3)=1/2, m=2. In P mode choose a tree under its original law, then choose a child uniformly. In Q mode choose it using Q1(t)=Z1(t)P1(t)/2, giving family weights 1/4,3/4 and Q1*(t,v)=P1(t)/2=1/4. Both modes choose a child uniformly conditional on the selected tree; only the tree weights change. Disk areas encode joint probabilities; edge lengths and positions stay fixed. Child buttons only move the mark. P already survives surely here, yet Q changes reproduction: size bias is not conditioning on survival. Only the first generation is illustrated; no infinite-level density dQ=W dP is asserted.</figcaption><nav class=\"ex-downloads\"><a href=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v1/E20.en.svg\">Complete static SVG</a><a href=\"/print/E20.en.html\">Print view</a></nav></figure>",
