      "title": "A clock change aligns; it does not erase",
      "html": "<figure class=\"explain-figure early-figure\" id=\"visual-E24\" data-early=\"E24\" lang=\"en\"><header><span>E24</span><h3>A clock change aligns; it does not erase</h3></header><p class=\"\">Match reference time a to original time a+δ. One jump aligns exactly; a pulse must still reach height 1.</p><div class=\"v5-controls\" role=\"group\"><button type=\"button\" data-path-mode=\"jump\" aria-pressed=\"true\">One jump</button><button type=\"button\" data-path-mode=\"pulse\" aria-pressed=\"false\">One pulse</button></div><div class=\"v5-controls\" role=\"group\"><button type=\"button\" data-delta=\"4\" aria-pressed=\"false\">δ=1/4</button><button type=\"button\" data-delta=\"8\" aria-pressed=\"true\">δ=1/8</button><button type=\"button\" data-delta=\"16\" aria-pressed=\"false\">δ=1/16</button></div><div class=\"early-flow\"><section><h4>Original / aligned</h4><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v1/E24-en-8-jump-0.svg\" alt=\"A later jump compared with the reference jump\" data-path-scene></section><div class=\"flow-arrow\">⇄</div><section><h4>Top: reference t; bottom: original λ(t)</h4><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v1/E24-en-clock-8.svg\" alt=\"Three matched time pairs including fixed endpoints\" data-clock-scene></section></div><div class=\"v5-controls\" role=\"group\"><button type=\"button\" data-aligned=\"0\" aria-pressed=\"true\">Original times</button><button type=\"button\" data-aligned=\"1\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Apply the clock</button></div><output data-reading>Unaligned: uniform error 1. Clock error δ=1/8 can align the jump.</output><figcaption id=\"visual-E24-end\">Let a=1/2 and 0&lt;δ≤1/4. For x=1_[a,1] and xδ=1_[a+δ,1], λ is piecewise linear through (0,0),(a,a+δ),(1,1), an increasing continuous homeomorphism. Then ‖λ−id‖∞=δ, xδ∘λ=x, but ‖xδ−x‖∞=1. The pulse zδ=1_[a+δ,a+δ+δ²) retains supremum 1 after every time homeomorphism, so cannot tend to zero in J1. One λ displays the surviving pulse; surjectivity proves the claim for all λ. Filled/open endpoints encode right-continuous values; vertical connectors are not interpolated paths. A convergence statement requires δ→0.</figcaption><nav class=\"ex-downloads\"><a href=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v1/E24.en.svg\">Complete static SVG</a><a href=\"/print/E24.en.html\">Print view</a></nav></figure>",
